-- title:
--   q-expansion of the Hecke correspondence T_ℓ on differentials
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid M$. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeBetaOneDefined M ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeOperator.html#L84), i.e. that the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ carries every element of the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionField M` $\subseteq\mathbb Q((q))$ of $X_1(M)$ into `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M (M*ℓ)`; assume further that a diamond automorphism at $\ell$ exists, namely a $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of `x1FunctionField M` with `IsDiamondAut M ℓ σ` (so $\ell$ and $M$ are coprime and, for ratios $f/g$ of weight-$k$ modular forms on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with integral $q$-expansions, the $q$-expansion of $\sigma(f/g)$ times the $\gamma$-slash $q$-expansion of $g$ equals that of $f$, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$ whose upper-left entry is $\equiv\ell \bmod M$), and that some automorphism of the base change `x1FunctionFieldBar M` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ restricts, via the coefficient embedding, to `diamondAut M ℓ`. Let $\omega$ be a Kähler differential of `x1FunctionFieldBar M` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $n\in\mathbb Z$. Write $\Theta$ for `diffQExp`, the $F$-linear $q$-expansion map on differentials obtained from the derivation $q\,d/dq$ on Laurent series. Then the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $\Theta$ applied to the correspondence attached to the pair $(\beta,\alpha)$ of degeneracy maps into `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M (M*ℓ))` — the trace along `heckeBetaOneBar` of the pull-back along the inclusion `heckeAlphaOneBar` — equals the coefficient of index $n\ell$ of $\Theta\omega$, plus $\ell$ times the coefficient of index $n/\ell$ (integer division) of $\Theta$ applied to the correspondence built from `diamondAutBar M ℓ` and the identity, the latter term being $0$ unless $\ell\mid n$.
--
--   This is the weight-two form of the classical formula $a_n(T_\ell f)=a_{n\ell}(f)+\ell\,a_{n/\ell}(\langle\ell\rangle f)$ for $\ell\nmid M$, here realised on Kähler differentials of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with $T_\ell$ given as the trace along the $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ degeneracy map of the pull-back along the inclusion. It feeds the construction of injective ring homomorphisms from the algebra generated by the Hecke and diamond operators on differentials into the corresponding algebra acting on cusp forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_coeff_diffQExp_correspondence_heckeBetaOneBar_heckeAlphaOneBar_of_not_dvd.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X1HeckeOperator
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X1Diamond
